meta {
  name: Get Supertrend Values
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/supertrend/AAPL?timespan=M1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timespan: M1
  ~length: 7
  ~factor: 3
  ~sessions: RTH
  ~bars: 50
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get Supertrend Values
  
  Computes the Supertrend indicator per bar so you can verify the values
  against the Webull chart across timeframes. This endpoint does NOT place
  orders — it is for inspection/validation only.
  
  Any US stock symbol works (the ticker need NOT be in the watchlist).
  
  ## Query
  - `length`   — ATR period (default 7).
  - `factor`   — ATR multiplier (default 3).
  - `timespan` — bar granularity (default M1). Supported: M1, M5, M15, M30,
    M60, M120, M240, D, W, M, Y.
  - `sessions` — trading sessions (comma-separated). Supported: RTH, PRE,
    ATH, OVN. Omit to use the configured default.
  - `count`    — number of bars to fetch (default = webull.trading.warmup-bars).
  - `bars`     — how many most-recent points to return (default 50; use 0 for all).
  
  ## Response (200)
  { ticker, length, factor, timespan, sessions, barsFetched,
    latestSupertrend, latestDirection, latestClose, returned,
    series: [ { timestamp, timestampEt, open, high, low, close,
                atr, supertrend, direction (UP|DOWN), flip } ] }
  
  Warm-up bars (before the first ATR at index length-1) have null
  atr/supertrend/direction. `flip` is true on the bar where direction changed.
  
  ## Verifying against Webull
  Set the chart's Supertrend to (length=7, factor=3) on the SAME timeframe and
  compare on COMPLETED bars. The most recent bar may still be forming, so if
  the last value looks off, compare the previous (completed) bar instead.
  
  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid length/factor/timespan/session, or not enough bars.
  - `502` — Webull market-data error.
  - `503` — no bars returned.
}
